export anchor TrackLanesStyle:
    number: 386
    screen: FitnessTracker
    name: Track lanes
    idea: Every measure runs as a lane on a night running track, with painted lane numbers at the start, white lane lines, a chequered finish at the goal and a runner chevron marking how far today has got.
    base: dark
    palette:
        infield: #0e1612, the page, the board text ground and the style sheet
        stand: #1d2a23, the header and the results board
        track: #3c1b15, every lane group, fields and list rows
        covered: #c8634a, the stripe for the part of a lane already run
        laneLine: #efe5da, lane lines, painted numbers, the finish chequer and today's number tile
        ink: #fbf4ec, text and results
        muted: #e3c4b5, units and rest labels on the track
        infieldMuted: #a9bfb2, labels on the infield and the board
        amber: #ffb84d, the runner chevron, Finished tag, primary button, links and focus
        onAmber: #2a1206, text on amber and on lane line
    type:
        Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, Arial for numbers,
        labels and headings, bold. Board figures are 40px, painted lane
        numbers 36px or 26px in small groups, results 26px, section titles
        22px caps tracked 0.06em, lane names 13px caps. Text uses Helvetica
        Neue, Arial, system-ui at 15px.
    layout:
        A dark green stand header with a small track oval mark and
        Brightwork Move, a pill switch of Today, Week and Plan with Today
        filled cream, and the date on the right, ruled below by a 4px cream
        line. The main area has two columns. Every lane group is a dark red
        rubber band with 3px cream lines above and below, square on the
        right and rounded like a track bend on the left. Each lane has a
        painted number cell closed by a 4px start line, the lane name in
        small caps, a thin covered stripe ending in an amber chevron, a
        chequered finish strip at the goal, and the result with its unit on
        the right. The left column holds Today's rings as lanes 1 to 3 and
        This week as lanes 1 to 7, one per day, with today's number on a
        cream tile, rest days as a dashed lane and the word rest, and a 0 to
        10 km scale below. The right column holds the Evening run as a
        results board with a cream frame, a Finished flag tag and four
        figures in a two by two grid, then Heart rate zones as five smaller
        lanes, then the Half marathon plan as two lanes for week 6 of 12 and
        tomorrow's 14 km long run, then Sleep as one lane with a moon number
        showing the deep share. Below 960px the columns stack. At 375px lane
        groups run to the right edge of the screen.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between sections, lanes 58px tall or 46px in small groups, a 32px page gutter.
    density: Medium. Seventeen lanes carry every figure, read left to right like a race.
    corners: Lane groups are square on the right and rounded like a bend on the left. Pills for buttons, nav and tags. 6px on the board.
    borders: 2px cream lane lines between lanes, 3px lines above and below each group, a 4px start line after the lane numbers.
    shadows: None. Painted lines only.
    icons:
        A runner chevron at the end of the covered stripe, a chequered
        finish at the goal, a flag on Finished, a dashed lane and the word
        rest for empty days, a moon for sleep and an arrow for the next
        session.
    focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
    tone: Race words such as Lane, Finished, Finish line is the goal, Longest lane and rest.
